      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-09-10T17:39:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "MultiStrOpt doesn\u0027t quite work. For example, pylibmc backend expects nested dict with some integer tunables, or even \u0027url\u0027 value is expected to be a list of host:port pairs. You can\u0027t get this with backend_argument. It can only provide raw string values. So since dogpile.cache backends expect arbitrary dicts, JSON value seems like a right fit. We can limit it to only dicts, for example, but we should support any values in them.",
      "parentUuid": "fa98f980_979fdf5e",
      "revId": "20c7750050763bf06bf648ba6bf9e8a8d490ce2c",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
